 "notes": "tolerance.tightest is a hand-computed check (narrowest stated tolerance band among the toleranced dimensions; general-tolerance block not counted). Sheet 1: notes 1-7 + reference views; title block DESC ATTRIBUTE 'HEATSINK, TOP', PREP 2015-01-27 T.A.MATUSKA, ENG ON FILE J.M.PISARIK, DWG NO 827-9999-906, REV '-' (single dash), SHEET 1 OF 3. Sheets 2 and 3: 'PART NO. 827-9999-906 / REV - / SHEET 2 (3)'. Material here is 6061-T6 PLATE to ASTM B205 (not T651 as on -904). No company / scale / projection; plot-stamp scale not recorded; title block not complete. Note 3 is a hexagon flag note. Note 4 carries profile of a surface .016 A B C. DIMENSIONS (55 with a value, all recorded, group complete): almost all boxed BASIC. The drawing has the two known omissions: '4X SR' in the side view is printed WITHOUT a value (not recorded — nothing to record), and the notch corner radius on sheet 3 has no dimension (the -904 sheet shows 'R.135'). Hole callouts: 'Ø.182 - .192 ↧.250 ± .010 / ⌴Ø.245 - .255 ↧.100 ±.010' and 'Ø.145 - .155 ↧.250 ± .010 / ⌴Ø.245 - .255 ↧.125 ±.010' (depths recorded as separate linear rows without a type). Chamfers are '5X .050 X .050' (front view) and '4X .050 X .050' (sheet 3), boxed basic, recorded as type 'chamfer' nominal .050 with count. '4X R.032 ±.010' has a small circle at the leader end. GD&T: position frames Ø.005 Ⓛ A B C on the 2X Ø.370-.380 and the 4X Ø.215-.225; Ø.005 Ⓜ A B C on the two counterbored holes and the 4X Ø.123-.133 (modifiers not in the match rows). Perpendicularity .010 A carries datum B; perpendicularity .010 A B carries datum C; angularity .008 A on the 45° chamfers; a stacked profile of a surface .016 / flatness .005 frame (no datum references) carries datum A, '4 SURFACES'. Datum feature symbols per occurrence: A twice (front view, side view '4X A'), B three times (top view, side view, sheet 3), C three times (top view, front view, sheet 3). Material / coating not complete (reader vocabulary); notes not complete (stamp, view labels, 'SEE SHEET 3', '4 SURFACES')."
